  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Find the missing factor in the sum of the first $14$ terms of the geometric series $7-35+175-\u22ef.$\n\nExpress your answer as a fraction (do not round your answer).\n\n${S}_{14}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (1-{5}^{14})$",
  "worked_solution": "Given a geometric series, the sum of the first $N$ terms is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term of the series and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nIn our case, ${a}_{1}=7.$ To find the value of $r,$ we find the ratio of the first two terms in the series:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-35}{7}=-5\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{1}=7,\\,N=14,$ and $r=-5$ into our formula, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{14} & =7\\cdot \\frac{1-(-5)^{14}}{1-(-5)} \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1-{5}^{14}}{1+5} \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1-{5}^{14}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\cdot (1-{5}^{14})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
